`[slug]`, `("title")` and `@@type{…}` are all optional and independent (§7.4).

###[slug-head]("Heading X")@@headingX{`slug-extras`, .fancy} Extras-routed heading

###[heading-y]("Heading Y")@@headingY{number: "auto"} Routed by the second marker

###[unrouted]@@unknownZ{.x} An unclaimed marker keeps the layer default

§7.4: no `[slug]` bracket, so `slug` is a slug of the text itself — the built-in
`<hN>` hides it (`slug` is a template-only read), an extract sees it.

## A plain heading without extras
